<p>At the Info Desk, you will be in direct contact with our attendees, answering all kinds of questions about the convention. Think "Where is the Dealers' Den?", "How does the Art Show auction work?", "I lost my badge, what do I do?" or "What events are happening right now?". No two shifts are the same. The Info Desk is usually prominently positioned in the entrance hall and is open during the convention from Wednesday to Saturday.</p>

<p>Being fluent in English is mandatory for this position, as you will be dealing with people from many different nationalities.</p>

<p>Your main tools are the conbook (no attendee reads that 😉) and an internal knowledge database. The Info Desk is also right next to our ConOps back office, where experienced team members and drinks are always available. You don't need to know everything by heart, you just need to know where to look.</p>

<p>No prior experience is needed. We provide manuals and process documentation for all positions. Experienced team members ("Council") and a Director on Duty are always available to help you during the convention.</p>

<p>While this ad is for the Info Desk, joining ConOps means you become part of the whole team. We encourage everyone to try different roles, you can pick your shifts across all our services using our self-scheduling tool. You're in control of your schedule. Pick the shifts that work for you, and we only step in if shifts still need filling. We expect around 4-5 hours per day you're at the convention, typically adding up to about 15-20 hours across the convention days (Wednesday to Saturday).</p>

<p>We ask our team members to arrive by Tuesday morning to help with setup and to be available on Sunday for teardown. Setup and teardown are an all-hands effort: regardless of your usual role, everyone pitches in. How much you contribute on those days is up to you, every pair of hands helps!</p>

<p>You must be a registered attendee of Eurofurence and meet the convention's minimum age requirement. There is no application deadline, you can reach out to us at any time. We'll have a short, informal chat to get to know each other and figure out where you'd fit best.</p>

<h3>Why join ConOps?</h3>

<ul>
    <li>Help make this convention happen. Eurofurence is entirely volunteer-run!</li>
    <li>Look behind the scenes and have the opportunity to influence how things are done</li>
    <li>Access to the staff lounge (with slushies, soft ice, cup noodles, real food, and more)</li>
    <li>Our own ConOps back office with drinks, exclusive to the team</li>
    <li>A small token of appreciation for every team member each year</li>
    <li>A great team with great team spirit</li>
</ul>

<h3>Interested in joining Con Operations?</h3>

<p>A simple "Hi, I'm interested!" is enough to get started, a short introduction about yourself is also welcome. Please send us an email to <a href="mailto:ConOps@Eurofurence.org" target="_blank">ConOps@Eurofurence.org</a> or contact <a href="https://t.me/FurryTeddyBear" target="_blank">@FurryTeddyBear on Telegram</a>. Email is slightly preferred for initial contact; we usually continue the conversation on Telegram. While we strongly prefer applications before the convention, feel free to reach out to us if you're interested, even on short notice.</p>
